  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With avatars 3.0 on the horizon exposing animation layers to users, I think it would be worth considering granting world creators the ability to dynamically add animation layers to player avatars within a world.\nIt's already possible to override player avatar animations using stations, but comprehensive, Udon-scriptable layers might be a better overall solution that is consistent with the way animation layers will be handled with avatars 3.0.\nFor example, an additional locomotion layer with the appropriate mask could override player locomotion animations with a swimming or flying animation.",
